LOCAL1="Sparky Stereo OS: a deb-multimedia package ships files of the edition's package under another name"
LOCAL2="%s from deb-multimedia ships files of the edition's %s under another name, so the edition ran its files instead of its own. apt had installed it by itself and nothing needs it: it was removed and %s was installed again, once. The edition's pin keeps apt from choosing it again."
LOCAL3="%s from deb-multimedia ships files of the edition's %s under another name. You installed it yourself, so it stays as you made it, and its files replace the edition's. To use the edition's own: sudo apt-get remove %s, then sudo apt-get install --reinstall %s."
LOCAL4="%s from deb-multimedia ships files of the edition's %s under another name. It stays: it is needed by %s. To use the edition's own, remove what needs it and %s, then sudo apt-get install --reinstall %s."
LOCAL5="%s failed with exit status %s: %s from deb-multimedia still ships files of the edition's %s under another name. Repair tries again."
LOCAL6="%s failed with exit status %s: %s was removed, but the edition's %s could not be installed again, so some of its files may be missing. Repair tries again."
LOCAL7="%s from deb-multimedia ships files of the edition's %s under another name. apt had installed it by itself and nothing needs it: it was removed. %s is not installed here, so nothing took its place."
